sequenceDiagram
  title: Order Processing - Event-Driven Saga Choreography

  participant User as Web Browser
  participant APIGateway as API Gateway
  participant OrderService as Order Service
  participant EventStore as Event Store Service
  participant Redis as Redis Pub/Sub
  participant OrderConsumer as Order Consumer
  participant MarketConsumer as Market Consumer
  participant UserConsumer as User Consumer

  %% PHASE 1: Synchronous Order Acceptance
  User->>APIGateway: POST /v1/orders with JWT
  APIGateway->>APIGateway: Validate JWT & request

  APIGateway->>OrderService: POST /v1/orders (create order)
  OrderService->>OrderService: Persist order with status PENDING
  OrderService-->>APIGateway: Order ID + PENDING status

  APIGateway->>EventStore: POST /v1/events (OrderCreated)
  EventStore->>EventStore: Save event in order_events table
  EventStore->>EventStore: Insert into outbox table (transactional)
  EventStore->>EventStore: Init saga_state (CREATED)
  EventStore-->>APIGateway: Event published

  APIGateway-->>User: 202 Accepted with order_id

  note over User,APIGateway: Synchronous phase complete - User can poll /v1/orders/:id

  %% PHASE 2: Asynchronous Event-Driven Saga
  note over EventStore,UserConsumer: Event-driven choreography (no central orchestrator)

  EventStore->>Redis: PUBLISH order_events (OrderCreated)
  
  %% Step 1: Validation
  Redis->>OrderConsumer: OrderCreated event
  OrderConsumer->>OrderConsumer: Check idempotency
  OrderConsumer->>OrderConsumer: Validate pre-trade
  
  alt Validation Failed
    OrderConsumer->>EventStore: POST /v1/events (OrderRejected)
    EventStore->>EventStore: Save event + outbox + saga_state (FAILED)
    EventStore->>Redis: PUBLISH order_events (OrderRejected)
    EventStore->>OrderService: Update order status to REJECTED
    note over OrderConsumer: Saga ends - order rejected
  else Validation Passed
    OrderConsumer->>EventStore: POST /v1/events (OrderValidated)
    EventStore->>EventStore: Save event + outbox + saga_state (VALIDATED)
    EventStore->>Redis: PUBLISH order_events (OrderValidated)
    OrderConsumer->>OrderConsumer: Mark event as processed
  end

  %% Step 2: Market Execution
  Redis->>MarketConsumer: OrderValidated event
  MarketConsumer->>MarketConsumer: Simulate market execution
  
  MarketConsumer->>EventStore: POST /v1/events (OrderExecuted or OrderPartiallyFilled)
  EventStore->>EventStore: Save event + outbox + saga_state (EXECUTED)
  EventStore->>Redis: PUBLISH order_events (OrderExecuted)

  %% Step 3: Order Status Update
  Redis->>OrderConsumer: OrderExecuted event
  OrderConsumer->>OrderConsumer: Check idempotency
  OrderConsumer->>OrderService: Update order status to FILLED
  OrderConsumer->>EventStore: Update saga_state (EXECUTED)
  OrderConsumer->>OrderConsumer: Mark event as processed

  %% Step 4: Settlement (User Balance & Holdings)
  Redis->>UserConsumer: OrderExecuted event
  UserConsumer->>UserConsumer: Calculate settlement
  UserConsumer->>UserConsumer: Update user balance in DB
  UserConsumer->>UserConsumer: Update holdings in DB
  
  UserConsumer->>EventStore: POST /v1/events (OrderCompleted)
  EventStore->>EventStore: Save event + outbox + saga_state (COMPLETED)
  EventStore->>Redis: PUBLISH order_events (OrderCompleted)

  %% Step 5: Final Status Update
  Redis->>OrderConsumer: OrderCompleted event
  OrderConsumer->>OrderConsumer: Check idempotency
  OrderConsumer->>EventStore: Update saga_state (COMPLETED)
  OrderConsumer->>OrderConsumer: Mark event as processed

  note over EventStore,UserConsumer: Saga completed - all services updated asynchronously

  %% USER POLLING
  User->>APIGateway: GET /v1/orders/:id
  APIGateway->>OrderService: GET /v1/orders/:id
  OrderService-->>APIGateway: Order with FILLED status
  APIGateway-->>User: Order details with execution results

  User->>APIGateway: GET /v1/me
  APIGateway->>UserConsumer: GET /v1/users/:id
  UserConsumer-->>APIGateway: User with updated balance & holdings
  APIGateway-->>User: Updated portfolio
